      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dayton%2C_Kentucky",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Dayton hosts an annual festival celebrating Mary Ingles, a pioneer woman who escaped from Shawnee Indians near Dayton in 1755.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dayton%2C_Kentucky",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A big sandbar off Dayton was the 1779 site of Rogers’ Defeat, where David Rogers and 70 men camped before heading upriver.",
